These libraries ship in vendor/. They stay under their own licenses and
are not relicensed:

- dompdf.js 2.0.7 — MIT License
  https://github.com/lmn1919/dompdf.js
  Draws the selectable PDF from the page on screen.

- pdf-lib 1.17.1 — MIT License
  https://github.com/Hopding/pdf-lib
  Attaches document.json to that PDF and reads the attachment back.
  It does not draw the page.

- Roboto, by Google — Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto
  A typeface for the page and the PDF, latin subset, via Fontsource.
  Screen files are in vendor/fonts. vendor/fonts.js holds the same
  bytes so the PDF can be built from disk.

- Merriweather, by Sorkin Type — SIL Open Font License 1.1
  https://github.com/SorkinType/Merriweather
  An optional typeface for the page and the PDF, latin subset, via Fontsource.

- Lora, by Cyreal — SIL Open Font License 1.1
  https://github.com/cyrealtype/Lora
  An optional typeface for the page and the PDF, latin subset, via Fontsource.

- Inter, by Rasmus Andersson — SIL Open Font License 1.1
  https://github.com/rsms/inter
  The typeface for the buttons and screens, latin subset, via Fontsource.

- Lucide icon shapes — ISC License
  https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide
  The stroke icons on the setup cards.

- SortableJS 1.15.6 — MIT License
  https://github.com/SortableJS/Sortable
  Shipped in vendor/. The editor reorders blocks with its own pointer code.

- Cropper.js 1.5.13 — MIT License
  https://github.com/fengyuanchen/cropperjs
  Frames and crops a photo inside the editor. vendor/cropper.min.js
  and vendor/cropper.min.css.
